# modules/iac/cloudformation.rules - CloudFormation YAML/JSON checks. precision.awk binds
# each candidate to its owning Resources entry, Type and Properties mapping,
# excluding Metadata and block scalar prose. KMS rotation inspects its complete
# Properties mapping, never neighboring keys or an arbitrary line window.
# Owns: docs/DESIGN.md §6.6/§8.2; docs/FOUNDATION.md tension 3 precision amendment.

id: IAC-CFN-OPEN_CIDR-01
title: CloudFormation security group ingress open to 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0
severity: high
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-284
owasp: A02:2025
pattern: "?Cidr(Ip|Ipv6)"?\s*:\s*"?(0\.0\.0\.0/0|::/0)"?
dialect: ere
files: *.yaml
files: *.yml
files: *.json
files: *.template
tags: static
tags: compliance
cis: 5.2
cis: 5.3
remediation: Restrict CidrIp/CidrIpv6 to the smallest network that needs access. Where
  public reachability is genuinely required (a public load balancer listener), terminate
  it at an edge that applies WAF and rate limiting rather than at the instance security
  group.
references: CIS-AWS-5.2

id: IAC-CFN-S3_PUBLIC_ACCESS-01
title: S3 bucket disables a public-access-block control, or sets a public canned ACL
severity: critical
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-284
owasp: A02:2025
pattern: "?(BlockPublicAcls|BlockPublicPolicy|IgnorePublicAcls|RestrictPublicBuckets)"?\s*:\s*"?[Ff]alse"?|"?AccessControl"?\s*:\s*"?[Pp]ublic-?[Rr]ead(-?[Ww]rite)?"?
dialect: ere
files: *.yaml
files: *.yml
files: *.json
files: *.template
tags: static
tags: compliance
cis: 2.1.4
remediation: Set every PublicAccessBlockConfiguration flag (BlockPublicAcls,
  BlockPublicPolicy, IgnorePublicAcls, RestrictPublicBuckets) to true and remove any
  public canned ACL. If the object truly must be public, front it with CloudFront and
  an Origin Access Control instead of a public bucket.
references: CWE-284
references: CIS-AWS-2.1.4

id: IAC-CFN-UNENCRYPTED-01
title: RDS or EBS resource explicitly configured without encryption at rest
severity: high
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-311
owasp: A04:2025
pattern: "?StorageEncrypted"?\s*:\s*"?[Ff]alse"?
dialect: ere
files: *.yaml
files: *.yml
files: *.json
files: *.template
tags: static
tags: compliance
remediation: Set StorageEncrypted to true and, where the resource supports it, pin a
  customer-managed KMS key via KmsKeyId rather than relying on the account default key.
references: CWE-311

id: IAC-CFN-KEY_ROTATION_DISABLED-01
title: KMS key resource declared without automatic key rotation enabled
severity: medium
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-320
owasp: A04:2025
pattern: "?Type"?\s*:\s*"?AWS::KMS::Key"?
dialect: ere
files: *.yaml
files: *.yml
files: *.json
files: *.template
tags: static
remediation: Add EnableKeyRotation: true to the AWS::KMS::Key resource so AWS rotates
  the backing key material annually without any application-visible change (KMS
  transparently keeps prior key material available for decrypting old ciphertext).
references: CWE-320
references: CIS-AWS-3.6
cis: 3.6

id: IAC-CFN-PUBLIC_IP-01
title: EC2 instance or launch template auto-assigns a public IP address
severity: high
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-284
owasp: A02:2025
pattern: "?AssociatePublicIpAddress"?\s*:\s*"?[Tt]rue"?
dialect: ere
files: *.yaml
files: *.yml
files: *.json
files: *.template
tags: static
tags: compliance
remediation: Set AssociatePublicIpAddress to false and reach the instance through a
  bastion, a VPN, or a load balancer in a public subnet instead of giving the instance
  itself a public address. If a public address is genuinely required, pair it with a
  security group scoped to specific source ranges, not 0.0.0.0/0.
references: CWE-284

id: IAC-CFN-HARDCODED_SECRET-01
title: Hardcoded credential literal in a CloudFormation resource property
severity: critical
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-798
owasp: A07:2025
pattern: \b(Password|Secret|SecretKey|ApiKey|AccessKey|Token|MasterUserPassword|ClientSecret)\b"?\s*:\s*"?[^"'!{\s][^"'\n]{7,}
dialect: ere
files: *.yaml
files: *.yml
files: *.json
files: *.template
tags: static
remediation: Remove the literal credential from the template and rotate it immediately;
  a committed secret must be treated as compromised even if the commit is later reverted,
  because it remains in git history. Source the value from an existing Secrets
  Manager/SSM SecureString resource via a dynamic reference
  ('{{resolve:secretsmanager:...}}' / '{{resolve:ssm-secure:...}}') instead of a literal.
references: CWE-798

id: IAC-CFN-RDS_PUBLIC-01
title: RDS instance configured as publicly accessible
severity: critical
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-284
owasp: A02:2025
pattern: "?PubliclyAccessible"?\s*:\s*"?[Tt]rue"?
dialect: ere
files: *.yaml
files: *.yml
files: *.json
files: *.template
tags: static
tags: compliance
cis: 2.3.3
remediation: Set PubliclyAccessible to false and reach the database through an
  application tier inside the same VPC, a bastion, or a VPN, never a public endpoint.
references: CWE-284
references: CIS-AWS-2.3.3

id: IAC-CFN-ECS_PRIVILEGED-01
title: ECS task definition runs a container with privileged escalation enabled
severity: critical
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-269
owasp: A02:2025
pattern: "?Privileged"?\s*:\s*"?[Tt]rue"?
dialect: ere
files: *.yaml
files: *.yml
files: *.json
files: *.template
tags: static
tags: compliance
remediation: Remove the Privileged property from the container definition (it defaults to
  false). A privileged ECS container gets near-complete access to the container instance -
  device nodes, kernel capabilities, and namespaces - so almost every real task can run
  instead with a narrow, explicit linuxParameters.capabilities.add list for only the
  capability it actually needs. On Fargate the property is not supported at all.
references: CWE-269
